# The McDonnell Douglas F-15C Eagle's checklists: this project's own words,
# following the aeroplane's own flight manual.
#
# **The source is T.O. 1F-15A-1**, the USAF flight manual for the F-15A, B, C
# and D from block 7 up, section II, Normal Procedures, pages 2-7 to 2-12, as
# scanned in the Internet Archive's copy at
# <https://archive.org/details/f-15-manual>. docs/ASSETS.md records it.
# What is below is that section's drills in this project's own words, cut
# down to what a simulated aeroplane can be seen to do: the manual's radar,
# IFF, INS alignment, ejection seat, canopy, oxygen and armament have nothing
# here that could show them done, and are the pilot's to confirm or are left
# out.
#
#   phase NAME                       one of: before-start, taxi, take-off,
#                                    climb, cruise, descent, approach,
#                                    landing, after-landing
#   check PROPERTY OP VALUE TEXT...  an item the aircraft can see done
#   range PROPERTY LOW HIGH TEXT...  the same, where a band shows it done
#   confirm TEXT...                  an item only the pilot can see done
#
# with `#` beginning a comment; src/sim/checklist.hpp owns the format.
#
# The model has no flap channel, so nothing here reads a flap setting even
# though the manual's drills turn on one: "Flaps - CHECK DOWN" before take-off
# and "Flaps - UP" after landing are the pilot's to confirm here. It does have
# a speedbrake lever, and the lever moves the surface, but the aerodynamics
# draws no drag from it yet, so the speedbrake items below say only where the
# lever is. Its two F100s light their reheat above a throttle of 0.99, which
# is what "into reheat" and "no reheat" mean here.
#
# **The manual has no angle-of-attack channel here to read.** Its approach is
# flown at on-speed AOA, 20 to 22 units, not at a speed; the speeds below are
# this project's own figures in assets/figures/f15c.xml, and the manual's own
# numbers are used where it gives them - 300 knots at the break, gear and
# flaps below 250, aerobraking above 90.

phase before-start
confirm Walk-round done and the aeroplane clear to start
confirm Strapped in, harness checked, and the ejection controls safety lever armed
confirm Oxygen quantity checked and the oxygen test done
confirm Armament master switch safe
check fcs/throttle-cmd-norm <= 0.05 Both throttles closed
check gear/gear-cmd-norm >= 0.95 Undercarriage lever down

phase taxi
check propulsion/engine[0]/n1 >= 35.0 Port engine running
check propulsion/engine[1]/n1 >= 35.0 Starboard engine running
check fcs/speedbrake-cmd-norm <= 0.05 Speedbrake in
confirm Brakes and nose wheel steering checked as the aeroplane first moves
check fcs/throttle-cmd-norm <= 0.40 Taxi at a walking pace on low power

phase take-off
# Before Takeoff, items 2 to 10, and the Takeoff paragraph.
range fcs/pitch-trim-cmd-norm -0.35 0.35 Take-off trim checked
check fcs/speedbrake-cmd-norm <= 0.05 Speedbrake in
confirm Flight controls checked free, and the flaps checked down
confirm Canopy closed and locked, and the pitot heat on
range propulsion/engine[0]/n1 75.0 101.0 Engines advanced to 80 per cent, instruments checked
check fcs/throttle-cmd-norm >= 0.90 Brakes released and the throttles up to military or maximum
check velocities/vc-kts >= 115.0 Half aft stick at about 120 knots, rotating to ten degrees

phase climb
# Climb Techniques: military power, 350 knots to 0.90 Mach.
check gear/gear-cmd-norm <= 0.05 Undercarriage lever up
check gear/gear-pos-norm <= 0.05 Undercarriage locked up
check fcs/speedbrake-cmd-norm <= 0.05 Speedbrake in
range velocities/vc-kts 300.0 400.0 Climbing at 350 knots until 0.90 Mach
confirm Engine instruments, cabin pressure, oxygen and fuel transfer watched

phase cruise
# Inflight: 0.90 Mach is what the military-power climb levels at.
range velocities/mach 0.75 0.92 Holding 0.90 Mach or below
range position/h-sl-ft 30000.0 45000.0 Level between 30,000 and 45,000 feet
check fcs/throttle-cmd-norm <= 0.99 Military power, no reheat
check gear/gear-pos-norm <= 0.05 Undercarriage up
confirm Internal against total fuel checked, and the transfer watched

phase descent
# Descent Check/Before Landing: the two items the manual lists.
check fcs/speedbrake-cmd-norm >= 0.50 Speedbrake out as required
range fcs/throttle-cmd-norm 0.0 0.60 Throttles back for the descent
check velocities/vc-kts <= 450.0 Down at no more than 450 knots
confirm Armament master switch safe, and the altimeter set

phase approach
# Normal Landing: 300 knots at the break, gear and flaps on downwind below
# 250, on final at on-speed angle of attack.
check gear/gear-cmd-norm >= 0.95 Undercarriage lever down on downwind, below 250 knots
check gear/gear-pos-norm >= 0.95 Undercarriage down and locked
check fcs/speedbrake-cmd-norm <= 0.05 Speedbrake in for the approach
range velocities/vc-kts 145.0 250.0 Speed reduced through the base turn to on-speed
confirm Flaps down with the undercarriage, below 250 knots
confirm On final at on-speed angle of attack, 20 to 22 units

phase landing
range velocities/vc-kts 135.0 160.0 Over the threshold on speed
check gear/gear-pos-norm >= 0.95 Undercarriage down and locked
check fcs/throttle-cmd-norm <= 0.25 Throttles smoothly to idle at the flare
confirm Nose raised to about thirteen degrees for aerodynamic braking, and not past fifteen
confirm Aerobraking first, above 90 knots, and the wheel brakes after it

phase after-landing
# After Landing, items 1 to 8.
check position/h-agl-ft <= 50.0 Down and rolling
check fcs/speedbrake-cmd-norm <= 0.05 Speedbrake in
check velocities/vc-kts <= 40.0 Clear of the runway and slowed to a taxi
check fcs/throttle-cmd-norm <= 0.35 Throttles back to a taxi power
range fcs/pitch-trim-cmd-norm -0.35 0.35 Trim returned to take-off
confirm Flaps up, and the ejection controls safety lever locked
